---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="DuBose, M.D. — direct primary care" bookbar={true}>

  <!-- 1 · Hero — typographic; candid photography arrives at launch -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Direct primary care &middot; [City], Texas</span>
          <h1>A doctor with time to actually figure it out with you.</h1>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="sub">
            I&rsquo;m a primary care physician with a small practice and
            unhurried visits — for people who want a doctor who knows them,
            listens carefully, and helps make sense of the whole picture.
          </p>
          <div class="cta-row">
            <a class="btn" href="/book">Book a free conversation</a>
            <a class="quiet" href="/how-it-works">How it works &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pstrip">
        <div><b>$100 a month</b>one flat price, no per-visit charges</div>
        <div><b>Cancel anytime</b>no contract, no sign-up fee</div>
        <div><b>Keeps your insurance</b>works alongside it, never instead of it</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2 · Recognition -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">The situation</span>
          <h2>If your health has started to feel like too much</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            Maybe it&rsquo;s several things at once — blood pressure creeping
            up, sleep that never feels like rest, results nobody fully
            explained, medications you&rsquo;re not sure you still need. Maybe
            you&rsquo;ve seen good specialists, and each one checked their
            part — but no one is looking at the whole of it, with you.
          </p>
          <p>
            Or maybe nothing is wrong yet. You&rsquo;d just like a doctor who
            knows you before something is.
          </p>
          <p>
            Either way, the problem usually isn&rsquo;t a lack of healthcare.
            It&rsquo;s that nobody has time to think it through with you.
          </p>
          <p><a class="quiet" href="/help">What I can help with &rarr;</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 · What I do -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">What I do</span>
          <h2>Medicine, given room to work</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            My job is to listen carefully, understand your whole situation —
            medical, and the life around it — figure out what&rsquo;s urgent,
            what matters most, and what can wait, and then work the plan with
            you over time. Visits are as long as they need to be. Between
            visits, you can message me and I&rsquo;ll answer — and every
            result comes with my explanation, not just a number.
          </p>
          <p>
            This isn&rsquo;t alternative medicine or a wellness program.
            It&rsquo;s evidence-based primary care with the one thing modern
            medicine rarely has: enough time.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4 · How it works, in four steps -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Membership</span>
        <h2>How it works</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step-item">
          <span class="num">01</span>
          <h4>We talk first</h4>
          <p>A free 30-minute video conversation. No pressure — if I&rsquo;m
          not the right fit, I&rsquo;ll say so.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <span class="num">02</span>
          <h4>You join if it fits</h4>
          <p>$100 a month. No sign-up fee, no contract. Cancel anytime.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <span class="num">03</span>
          <h4>Care that fits you</h4>
          <p>Mostly by video. I come to you when an exam truly needs it;
          clinic space when that&rsquo;s better.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <span class="num">04</span>
          <h4>You see it working</h4>
          <p>Your trends — blood pressure, labs, how you feel — visible to
          both of us, so we know it&rsquo;s worth it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:36px"><a class="quiet" href="/how-it-works">The details, start to finish &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5 · The price, plainly -->
  <section class="section band-tint" id="bookbar-after">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Pricing</span>
        <h2>The price, plainly</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="split even" style="align-items:start">
        <div class="price-card">
          <div class="amt">$100 <span>/ month per adult</span></div>
          <div class="per">no per-visit charges</div>
          <ul class="check-list">
            <li>Visits as your care needs them</li>
            <li>Direct messaging with me</li>
            <li>Every result explained</li>
            <li>Your care coordinated</li>
            <li>Forms and paperwork handled</li>
            <li>Home visits when needed</li>
            <li>Cancel anytime</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <h3>What it doesn&rsquo;t cover</h3>
          <p style="margin-top:8px">
            Labs, imaging, medications, vaccines, specialists, hospitals —
            your insurance keeps covering those, like today.
          </p>
          <h3 style="margin-top:28px">On Medicare or Medicaid?</h3>
          <p style="margin-top:8px">
            You can still join — one extra form handles it.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top:24px"><a class="quiet" href="/pricing">Pricing &amp; how insurance fits &rarr;</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6 · Honest fit -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Honest fit</span>
        <h2>Who this is for — and who it isn&rsquo;t</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="fit">
        <div>
          <h3>A good fit if&hellip;</h3>
          <ul class="yes">
            <li>you want a doctor who actually knows you</li>
            <li>your health feels tangled and you want help sorting it out</li>
            <li>you&rsquo;re managing ongoing conditions and want them truly
            managed, not just refilled</li>
            <li>you&rsquo;d rather prevent problems than chase them</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Not a fit if&hellip;</h3>
          <ul class="no">
            <li>you need 24/7 physician access — I keep business hours and
            take real time off, and I&rsquo;ll always tell you how care works
            while I&rsquo;m away</li>
            <li>you&rsquo;re looking for emergency or hospital care —
            that&rsquo;s the ER&rsquo;s job, and it never stops being the
            ER&rsquo;s job</li>
            <li>you&rsquo;re under 18 — I care for adults only</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="soft" style="margin-top:28px">I&rsquo;d rather be clear about this now than disappoint you later.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 7 · The doctor -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-grid">
        <div class="photo-frame">
          <div class="photo" style="aspect-ratio:1/1">
            <img src="/images/dr-dubose-square.jpg" alt="Dr. Logan DuBose" width="640" height="640" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <span class="eyebrow">The doctor</span>
          <h2>Logan DuBose, M.D.</h2>
          <p style="margin-top:16px">
            I&rsquo;m a physician and researcher. I built this practice after
            years of studying why healthcare fails people: because I kept
            meeting patients who didn&rsquo;t need more healthcare — they
            needed one doctor with enough time to think.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top:20px"><a class="quiet" href="/about">More about me and how I practice &rarr;</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 8 · Common questions -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Questions</span>
          <h2>Common questions</h2>
          <p style="margin-top:18px"><a class="quiet" href="/questions">All questions, answered &rarr;</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq">
        <details>
          <summary>Is this health insurance?</summary>
          <p class="a">
            No. It is a direct agreement between you and me for my services
            as your physician. It does not replace insurance, and I recommend
            every member keep coverage for everything outside our
            relationship — labs, medications, specialists, hospitals.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Why is it only $100 when concierge doctors charge thousands?</summary>
          <p class="a">
            The price works because the practice is small by design: no
            office building, no billing department, no staff, and a limited
            number of patients. Concierge fees typically run $2,400 to $5,000
            a year on top of insurance billing; this is $100 a month, and I
            bill no one.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>I already have doctors I like — does this still make sense?</summary>
          <p class="a">
            Often, yes. You can keep every doctor you have — including
            another primary care physician. Members in that situation use me
            as the doctor who has time: to explain, to coordinate, to watch
            the whole picture between everyone else&rsquo;s appointments.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What&rsquo;s the catch?</summary>
          <p class="a">
            The limits are stated rather than hidden: I keep business hours,
            I am not an emergency service, I take real time away each year,
            and when my panel is full it is full. That is the whole catch.
          </p>
        </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 9 · Closing invitation -->
  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="inner">
        <h2>Start with a conversation. That&rsquo;s all.</h2>
        <p>
          Thirty minutes, by video, free. Tell me what&rsquo;s going on;
          I&rsquo;ll tell you honestly whether I can help — and if I&rsquo;m
          not the right fit, I&rsquo;ll point you toward someone who is.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn-inverse" href="/book">Book a free conversation</a>
        <div class="signup">
          <p>
            Not ready to talk? Leave your email and I&rsquo;ll send an
            occasional letter about the practice — no more than monthly,
            never a sales sequence.
          </p>
          <form action="#" method="post">
            <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="email address" aria-label="Email address" required />
            <button class="btn btn-inverse" type="submit">Send me the letter</button>
          </form>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
